WEBVTT

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.490
Enemy force eliminated!

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.490
<b>Southern Kingdom of Soleil, State of Leo Tacrath
State Capital Edinell</b>

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.190
<i>If we act now, we and the 
Excessarca can execute</i>

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.760
<i>a pincer attack on their 
retreating main force.</i>

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.600
Don't.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.000
Follow the plan. Don't pursue them.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.150
<i>Your Highness...</i>

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.930
Pointless battles create 
pointless sacrifices.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.040
Our forces are depleted enough as they are.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.640
We need to preserve as many as we can.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:37.710
<i>But—</i>

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.090
That's an order.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.020
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.240
The Price of Smiles

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.240
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:22.410
<b><i>The Final Message</i></b>

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.600
<i>It's been two and a half months 
since we fled the palace.</i>

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.260
<i>Despite our overwhelming disadvantage,</i>

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.610
<i>Princess Yuki has stymied our 
enemies' southward advance.</i>

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.500
<i>To secure the supplies needed 
for their prolonged campaign,</i>

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.200
<i>the Imperial Army continues to raid food 
plants and arsenals in Royal territory.</i>

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.660
<i>But Princess Yuki reacts quickly,</i>

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.240
<i>changing her tactics in response 
to intelligence received.</i>

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.760
<i>When we possess superior 
forces, she fights back.</i>

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.430
<i>When we don't, she withdraws 
without hesitation,</i>

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.430
<i>abandoning land and facilities...</i>

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.840
<i>...but only after evacuating the 
people and resources in advance.</i>

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.770
<i>As a result, the Imperial Army 
continues to expend resources</i>

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.290
<i>to capture land that gains them nothing.</i>

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.570
<i>When the Imperial Army withdraws, 
we can simply retake that area.</i>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.340
<i>Day in and day out, Princess Yuki 
pores over tactical guides,</i>

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.540
<i>learning how to fight in ways 
that best suit her ideals.</i>

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.700
James, Margrave Guize 
of the State of Chrisant

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.490
has submitted a request for aid.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:25.550
<i>Oh?</i>

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.700
I want you to take Yuni and Lune 
on the Excessarca to help them.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.190
We'll incorporate the State of Chrisant 
into our planning from here on out.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:39.110
<i>Didn't Margrave Guize say he 
would never serve a princess</i>

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.820
<i>who abandoned her people 
and fled the palace?</i>

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.300
He was just trying to 
fulfill his obligations.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:51.080
And it is true that I fled the palace.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.180
<i>Very well.</i>

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.710
<i>We'll set course for the State of Chrisant.</i>

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.290
Thank you.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.820
Maintain your presence, even here.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.720
Sorry!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.470
Your Highness.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.040
I have returned.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.580
Welcome back, Harold.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.730
Could I have a moment of your time?

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:25.240
We are working swiftly to increase 
production and installation of the new chrars.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.740
I believe we should strike 
the moment they're ready.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.680
Your Highness, no matter 
how long we hold out here,

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.100
they will never give up.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.690
The nature of war is that it does not end

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.630
until one side achieves its objectives.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.510
Maybe not, but...

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:50.890
I will do all I can to maintain 
morale on all fronts.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:53.770
In the meantime, 
please consider what I've said.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.270
Advisor Langford.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.710
You honor me with your presence.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.300
Don't take this personally.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:32.790
I've received word that those who've 
lost patience with the deadlock

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.310
are hoping to send a message with your death.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.740
I'll have you transferred to 
the motherland in a few days.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.290
Until then, I'll be keeping 
you isolated here.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.060
Understandable. I've been a 
completely worthless prisoner.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.830
But despite it all, I'm glad 
to have been brought here.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.330
What exactly do you mean by that?

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:58.300
I've guided countless guests 
to these quarters before,

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.090
but I've never been able to use them myself.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:06.860
If you could give us just one 
useful piece of information,

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.590
they'd lose the backing for 
their hardline approach.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:13.720
I'm afraid I lack any such resource.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.900
You'll be taken to the homeland the 
moment preparations are finished.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.700
Do try to make your last days 
in your homeland worthwhile.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.840
I hope the baby will come soon!

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:39.340
Your father did the same thing 
when I was pregnant with you.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:40.250
He did?

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.710
He hung off me even more, actually.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.660
No way!

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.150
Noel, would you?

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:52.340
Coming!

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.600
Good evening, Noel.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.100
You ditched work again!

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:02.600
Hey. It's not like I do it <i>that</i> often...

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.660
Princess Yuki.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:09.280
I thought we'd have a big meal, all together!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:25.790
Yes!

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:31.300
I... I meant to do that!

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.450
You know? It's really 
hard to cut it like this!

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.050
P-Princess Yuki, please allow me...

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.910
No! I said <i>we'd</i> make it today!

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.780
You need to relax, Elisa!

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:45.650
Yeah, Mom! You gotta do 
what the princess says!

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:49.170
But still...

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.310
Do not worry, Elisa.

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:54.280
I'll keep a <i>very</i> close eye on her.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:07:59.910
So good!

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.170
Miss Layla came up with the dishes.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:07.920
She said it's important that you 
eat a balanced meal at this stage.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:12.500
It would have turned out better if we 
could grow vegetables more reliably...

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.470
I never knew about it either...

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.930
Apparently, the crops haven't been 
growing well these last few years...

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:23.690
That's right. Izana has had concerns 
about that for some time, as well.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:24.780
Yes.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:30.110
He said we needed the new chrars 
to increase crop productivity.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.870
I see. Izana said that?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:38.290
When Dad gets back, I'll tell him 
I made dinner with Princess Yuki!

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.110
He'll be so surprised!

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:40.830
Right?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.160
Yes, that's right.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.430
I'm sure he'll be fine.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.420
He's much tougher than he looks.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:01.930
Getting Izana back is another reason 
we need to stop the war soon.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:04.650
I understand what Harold is saying...

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.550
but I'd like to avoid any more sacrifices.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.580
On their side, and on ours.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.690
Also...

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.520
Miss Layla, the day we left the palace...

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.530
That recording you showed me
 from twelve years ago...

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.710
I can't stop thinking about it.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.300
Izana left this for me?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.710
Yes. He said it was time 
for you to know the truth.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:34.720
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.970
<i>We've planted bombs in 
the hall and on the device.</i>

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.330
<i>I don't want to take innocent lives.</i>

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.520
<i>Dismantle the new chrars.</i>

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.820
<i>That power doesn't belong in this world!</i>

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.600
What does it mean?

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:52.110
You mean my parents didn't 
die in an accident?

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.610
The ones who attacked during the ceremony

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:01.370
were survivors of the old Empire of Verde.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.380
Yes.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.910
It seems that even before the incident,

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.370
they had been protesting the 
very existence of chrars.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:12.130
But Soleil and Grandiga 
did not share their views.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.620
That tragedy was the result.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:19.740
But none of you... not you, 
not Harold, nor Izana...

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.540
were told why they objected.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:27.890
Why did the Empire of Verde 
hate the new chrars so much?

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:54.780
<i>...the result of reviewing...</i>

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.700
<i>...defeat the Kingdom...</i>

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.470
<i>...in live combat.</i>

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.970
<i>...heat suppression remains 
insufficient for practical use,</i>

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.560
<i>so we're running further operational tests.</i>

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.640
<i>Perfection is not required.</i>

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.110
<i>Deploy them at once.</i>

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.230
<i>You can acquire data from live combat.</i>

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.370
<i>Very well.</i>

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:20.100
<i>But first, please give me one more chance.</i>

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:24.540
<i>I will defeat the Kingdom 
without using the new chrars.</i>

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.960
<i>Chief of Staff Eine Fleet,</i>

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:31.000
<i>is your reluctance to use the new chrars</i>

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:35.030
<i>the result of reviewing the 
Empire of Verde's research?</i>

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.670
The Empire of Verde?

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:50.550
How many can we install right now?

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:51.890
Twenty-four.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.340
Hurry.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.260
I want our preparations to be perfect.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.650
<i>Urgent message from recon squad.</i>

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.510
<i>The Imperial Army at the palace 
is showing signs of movement.</i>

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:06.080
Understood.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:07.850
I'll return to headquarters at once.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:14.590
Our recon squad reports five enemy 
carriers in port at the palace.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:17.170
They're probably about to send a large force.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:21.380
Their target will be one of 
these as-yet unoccupied states:

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:23.800
North Robia or Theras.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.210
What's the status of the Excessarca?

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:30.990
Still in the State of Chrisant, 
fighting alongside Margrave Guize's army.

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:32.810
I see.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:39.020
I have twenty-four Gards equipped 
with new chrars heading our way.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.440
We should muster our forces 
and meet them in battle.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:44.460
No.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.100
We'll continue our current strategy.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.330
They outnumber us too greatly.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.410
Prepare for withdrawal.

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:56.380
Losing either of those states will make it 
harder to hold off an attack on this city!

00:12:57.970 --> 00:12:59.410
That doesn't matter.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:00.970
As long as our people are safe,

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.380
there will always be another opportunity.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:03.380
Your Highness!

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:04.970
I will not change my plan!

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:09.850
Contact the armies in both states covertly.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.400
Have them ready to move people 
and resources at any time.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:15.070
Yes, ma'am...

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:31.430
Mom?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.080
Mom!

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.440
Message from the scout squad!

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.650
The enemy ships are setting out!

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.980
They're heading for the State of North Robia!

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:43.450
Move the people and resources of North Robia

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.260
along the designated routes 
to the State of Theras!

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.010
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:49.510
I'll have them mobilize at once!

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.030
Excuse me. Could I ask your opinion?

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.480
It's about baby names.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.570
I've narrowed it down to two,

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.940
but I can't seem to decide.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:30.090
Our forces will reach the State 
of Theras border momentarily.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.360
Five enemy carriers have arrived on the 
border to the State of North Robia.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.100
I think we're going to make it...

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.730
Princess Yuki! Message from an enemy ship!

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.560
Put them through.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:47.030
<i>I'm honored to speak with 
you again, Miss Yuki.</i>

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.530
You're...

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:50.780
<i>First, I'd like to apologize.</i>

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:55.270
<i>I spoke to you in our last 
meeting with contempt.</i>

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.290
<i>But I respect your continuing efforts,</i>

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:02.190
<i>and your ability to inspire 
loyalty in your people.</i>

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.420
Is this the only reason you called me?

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.520
<i>I wish to ask you one thing:</i>

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:10.300
<i>would you agree to surrender?</i>

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:13.610
<i>If you surrender now,</i>

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:17.470
<i>we can put an end to all of this 
without further loss of life.</i>

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:21.670
Twelve years ago,

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.760
the Empire of Verde resorted to terrorism

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:26.410
to keep the new chrars from being used.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.240
Does your empire know why?

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:31.990
I see that you do.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.200
If we surrender now, will you 
guarantee the safety of my people,

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:42.350
and the release of information 
about the Empire of Verde?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.710
<i>I will guarantee the former,</i>

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:49.090
<i>but on the latter, I refuse.</i>

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.840
Then I cannot agree to surrender.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:56.300
<i>A pity.</i>

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.410
<i>Then you should have focused less on that,</i>

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:02.520
<i>and more on your brethren 
just outside my front door.</i>

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.060
Message from the recon squad in Theras.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.400
Enemy ships and theurgears in large 
numbers are approaching from Rothea!

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.700
It looks like an ambush!

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.600
They anticipated our movements?

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.930
Of course... no time to keep eyes 
on a prisoner who's past usefulness.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.970
Urgent message! It's from 
Yuni Vanquish of the Order!

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.370
<i>Princess Yuki.</i>

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.300
<i>Yuni! Where are you?</i>

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.230
<i>Near the border between Rothea and Theras.</i>

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:26.040
<i>After we finished our mission,</i>

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.940
<i>we heard about the situation there, 
and we went on ahead of the Excessarca.</i>

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:34.570
<i>Our forces are surrounded 
about 300 meters away.</i>

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.200
Lune, do you know if they're all right?

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.710
<i>According to communications 
recon intercepted,</i>

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:42.260
<i>they've been completely wiped out.</i>

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.760
Your Highness!

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:46.830
I know...

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.340
I'm sorry. I'm all right.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.880
<i>Princess Yuki, recon picked up 
one more piece of information.</i>

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:01.560
<i>Their chief of staff, Eine Fleet, 
is in the ship ahead of us.</i>

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:05.240
<i>We could catch them by surprise right now.</i>

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.060
<i>I'm positive we could take that ship down.</i>

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.190
But... if you do that...

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.690
<i>We'd gladly give our lives to 
punch the Empire in the nose.</i>

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.070
You can't!

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:16.450
<i>Princess Yuki.</i>

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:21.630
<i>Losing their chief of staff will 
be a massive blow to their army.</i>

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.230
<i>Let us do this!</i>

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:24.830
I said no!

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:27.790
Princess, now is the time 
to do what is necessary!

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.630
We can't afford to lose 
any more of our people!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.500
After all this, you're still saying that?!

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.300
This is the only way I can do things!

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.100
It can't be...

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.770
Urgent message.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.560
This time it's from the palace!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.310
Izana?

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:57.860
What are you doing?!

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:02.240
Princess Yuki, I'm going to send 
you some extremely important data.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:03.220
<i>Data?</i>

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.270
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:05.830
<i>If they find you, they'll kill you!</i>

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:06.830
I know that.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:07.410
<i>Then...</i>

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:11.040
This data will change Soleil's future.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.280
<i>This contains the chrars research report</i>

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.760
<i>compiled by Empire of Verde scientists.</i>

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.760
The Empire of Verde...

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:27.520
It should show you what caused 
the incident twelve years ago.

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:33.980
<i>Izana!</i>

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:38.740
Izana!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:42.840
Your Highness! Grant permission to attack!

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:43.900
<i>Harold...</i>

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.260
<i>We can't have you going to pieces.</i>

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:53.630
<i>I've named our child about 
to be born. Tell Elisa...</i>

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:57.610
<i>"Ciel."</i>

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.300
<i>It's a word that means "sky" 
in our homeworld's language.</i>

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:07.990
<i>Boundless and vast... 
with unlimited freedom...</i>

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:14.200
<i>Tell my child... to live... that way...</i>

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.620
Izana! What are you talking about?

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:20.010
You know I can't do that!

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:24.160
You have to tell her yourself!

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:28.350
You have to name it yourself!

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:31.790
<i>You ask the unreasonable... 
to the very end...</i>

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:36.170
Izana...

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.180
Next time we meet, let's go for a drink.

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.940
Izana!

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:55.220
Elisa...

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:00.730
Princess Yuki! I have a little brother!

00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:02.560
I'm a big sister!

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:05.570
Princess Yuki, would you like to hold him?

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:19.960
Princess Yuki, are you crying?

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.140
<b><i>The Elegy of Dawn</i></b>
